3. Oil tops $90
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Financial Modeling Prep ; Chart: Emily Peck/Axios The price of U.S. benchmark crude oil futures has topped $90 a barrel for the first time since July, after the U.S. launched an attack on Iranian targets in the Strait of Hormuz.

 The big picture: Investors are growing even more concerned with diesel prices — at their highest level in more than four months and up more than 50% from June, FactSet analysts note.

 It's a key input for virtually anything grown or transported throughout the U.S., and puts huge pressure on inflation, as Matt wrote last month . 
 
 
